      "openaiSpec": {
        "name": "natural_language_search",
        "description": "CRITICAL GROUNDING TOOL: Executes intelligent web search and evidence extraction through an internal Gemini model pipeline. Use this as your primary engine for real-time fact retrieval, code syntax/examples, troubleshooting error codes, breaking changes, contradiction audits, and multi-step technical procedures.\n\nHOW TO QUERY: Express your retrieval objective as a complete, descriptive natural language sentence explaining what you need to find or verify (e.g., 'Compare performance tradeoffs between library X and Y in 2026' or 'Troubleshoot Windows 11 audio latency driver dropouts and find registry fixes'). DO NOT send keywords or boolean query strings; an internal Gemini 3.5 Flash-Lite router model interprets your natural language intent to formulate optimal multi-branch search queries.\n\nWHAT IT RETURNS: The tool returns structured artifacts (exact code, commands, steps, tables), claims with citation lineage, an epistemic control layer with confidence ratings, and explicit lists of missing facets.\n\nAPI ERROR HANDLING: If this tool returns an 'api_error' object, a 'completion_state' of 'failed', or an upstream status error (such as HTTP 401 Invalid Key, HTTP 402 Insufficient Balance, or HTTP 429 Rate Limit), you are STRICTLY FORBIDDEN from claiming 'no results were found'. You MUST report the exact error diagnostic, HTTP status code, and message directly to the user.",
        "parameters": {
          "type": "object",
          "properties": {
            "query": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "The retrieval objective expressed as a natural, descriptive sentence of your complete goal (e.g., 'Compare tradeoffs between X and Y' or 'How to resolve driver latency error 0x...'). DO NOT write short keywords or robotic search phrases. Expressing full context allows the internal router model to correctly classify your intent into specialized retrieval lanes and execute optimized parallel search tracks."
            },
            "detailMode": {
              "type": "string",
              "description": "Overrides retrieval breadth and extraction intensity. Use 'AUTO' to let the router choose. Use 'MINIMAL' for quick, single-source facts. Use 'EXHAUSTIVE' to pull high-density results across broad context windows (up to 60k+ chars, perfect for detailed lists, tables, or multi-part migrations). Use 'RAW_TEXT' when you need untouched, verbatim segments or raw source chunks.",
              "enum": [
                "AUTO",
                "MINIMAL",
                "EXHAUSTIVE",
                "RAW_TEXT"
              ]
            },
